  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the key finding chain:\n\n**Primary dead-code reference (high confidence, load-bearing):**\n- `packages/react-dom/src/client/ReactDOMLegacy.js` (React 18.2.0) defines `render()` and `unmountComponentAtNode()`, both gated behind `__DEV__` console.error deprecation warnings stating \"is no longer supported in React 18.\"\n- `packages/react-error-overlay/src/iframeScript.js` (CRA) imports `ReactDOM` from plain `'react-dom'` (not `react-dom/client`) and calls `ReactDOM.render(renderedElement, iframeRoot)` / `ReactDOM.unmountComponentAtNode(iframeRoot)` to mount/dismiss the dev build-error and runtime-error overlay UI.\n- This is wired in via `packages/react-dev-utils/refreshOverlayInterop.js` \u2192 `react-error-overlay`'s `reportRuntimeError`/`dismissRuntimeErrors`, which is load-bearing for react-scripts' dev-server error overlay.\n- Confirmed by `packages/react-error-overlay/package.json`, which still pins `\"react\": \"^17.0.2\"` / `\"react-dom\": \"^17.0.2\"` as devDependencies \u2014 the overlay is prebuilt against React 17's legacy render API rather than React 18's `createRoot`/`root.unmount()`, even though the rest of react-scripts 5.0.1 targets React 18.\n\n**Secondary vestigial reference (medium confidence):**\n- `packages/react-scripts/fixtures/kitchensink/template/src/index.js`, an internal e2e-test fixture, still does `import ReactDOM from 'react-dom'; ReactDOM.render(<App />, ...)` \u2014 contrasted with `packages/cra-template/template/src/index.js` and `cra-template-typescript/template/src/index.tsx`, which correctly use `ReactDOM.createRoot(...).render(...)` from `react-dom/client`. Not shipped to end users, but shows the deprecated API is still alive inside CRA's own test infrastructure.\n\n**Ruled out:** `unstable_batchedUpdates`, `unstable_createPortal`, `createFactory`, `react-dom/test-utils`, and `__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED` are all still exported by React 18.2.0 and had zero references anywhere in create-react-app \u2014 no dead-code hits there. The babel JSX-runtime detection (`hasJsxRuntime`) and webpack config correctly auto-select the modern `automatic` JSX transform, so no classic-runtime dead code was found in the build pipeline itself.",
